## Wire Modals

- `rishadblack/wire-modals` mounts Livewire components on demand and drives Bootstrap 5 modals declared in the component's own view: a trigger mounts the component the first time it is clicked, calls an action on it, keeps it alive while its modal is open and unmounts it when the modal closes. Activate the `wire-modals-development` skill whenever you create, edit or test a component that uses this package.
- Three building blocks: `<livewire:wire-modals.host />` once per layout, the `Rishadblack\WireModals\Traits\WithModals` trait on the component, and a trigger element `<button wire:modal="modals.note-edit" wire:modal.action="openNoteModal" wire:modal.id="@{{ $note->id }}" data-folder="inbox">`. The browser script must be imported after Livewire (`import '../../vendor/rishadblack/wire-modals/resources/js/wire-modals.js'`) and Bootstrap 5 must be on `window.bootstrap`.
- A trigger may only call a public method named `open*Modal` (config `action_patterns`) or marked `#[Rishadblack\WireModals\Attributes\ModalAction]`. Livewire and package methods are never callable. Mark one method `#[ModalAction(default: true)]` so triggers without an action land there. `wire:modal="alias@@action"` is a shorthand.
- Actions receive one array: `id`, `data` (every `data-*` attribute, kebab → snake, all strings), `action`, `component`, `modal`, `key`. Treat `id` and `data` as request input: load records yourself and authorise in the action or in the `authorizeModalAction(string $action, array $payload): bool` hook.
- Inside an action call `$this->modalOpen('NoteModal')`. The modal is `<x-wire-modals::modal id="NoteModal">` in the component's view and the `id` must match. `modalClose('NoteModal')` hides it; closing a modal opened with `modalOpen()` unmounts the component. Use `modalOpen('OptionsModal', keepComponent: true)` for sub-modals that must not unmount the parent. `closeComponent()` unmounts explicitly (open modals are hidden first).
- Build trigger attributes on the server with `<x-wire-modals::trigger component="..." action="..." :record-id="$id" :data="[...]">` or `Rishadblack\WireModals\Support\Trigger::make(...)` / `NoteEdit::modalTrigger('openNoteModal')->id($id)` (for table action columns). Never concatenate ids into markup by hand.
- A second click while the component is mounted re-enters it (the action runs again on the same instance). Two instances of one component need different `wire:modal.key` values.
- Only registered Livewire components that use the trait and match `allowed_components` can be mounted; the host keeps at most `max_mounted` components; `data` is capped by `max_payload_bytes`. Rejections are logged (`log_rejections`) and dispatch a `wire-modals:rejected` browser event. Config: `php artisan vendor:publish --tag=wire-modals-config`.
- Legacy mode (`legacy.events`, `legacy.directive`, `WithLegacyEvents` trait) exists only for applications migrating from a hand-rolled loader; do not use it in new code.
- Test with Pest: `Livewire::test('wire-modals.host')->call('load', ['component' => 'modals.note-edit', 'id' => $id])` and `Livewire::test('modals.note-edit', ['wireModalsPayload' => [...]])`, asserting `wire-modals:open` (`modal`, `owner`), `wire-modals:close`, `wire-modals:dispose` (`target`) and `wire-modals:rejected`.
